 Once the completion tokens are parsed, the requested function call is written out to the
 queue, after which the function executor (‘FE’) attempts to execute the requested function
 call. The output of the function call is then written out to the queue; if the function call
 resulted in a runtime error, an error message is returned. If the function execution resulted
 in an error or the LLM requested follow-up invocation, the logic loop restarts, otherwise, the
